BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shinjuku Boys | A Dykeumentary Night Screening
DTSTART:20261118T193000
DTEND:20261118T193000
UID:9f3492242500ab57eb1a4f3ca4283e3a@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:A film exploring the lives of three non-binary or transgender 
 men who work at the New Marilyn Club in Tokyo\, Japan. Dykeumentary Night 
 is a monthly lesbian movie night in Toronto. This month&#x27\;s film is Sh
 injuku Boys. OVERVIEW This documentary from Kim Longinoto and Jano William
 s (DREAM GIRLS)\, offers rich insight into gender and sexuality in Japan v
 ia a candid portrait of Kazuki\, Tatsu\, and Gaish\, three trans masculine
  hosts working at the New Marilyn Club in Tokyo’s bustling Shinjuku dist
 rict. As the film follows them at home and on the job\, all three (who sel
 f-describe themselves as onabe) talk frankly about their lives\, revealing
  their views on love\, sex\, sexual orientation\, traditional relationship
 s\, and identity. Alternating with these illuminating interviews are fabul
 ous sequences shot inside the club\, a place patronized largely by heteros
 exual\, cisgender women. Chicago Film Festival\, Silver Hugo Houston Film 
 Festival\, Gold Prize SF Lesbian and Gay Film Festival\, Outstanding Docum
 entary London Film Festival NY Lesbian and Gay Film Festival Honolulu Lesb
 ian and Gay Film Festival Sydney Lesbian and Gay Film Festival One Gallery
 \, CA Reykjavik Shorts&amp\;Docs Festival OutFest Los Angeles Doors: 7:30 
 PM Screening: 8:00 PM ‍
LOCATION:Three Dollar Bill\, 1592 Queen Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/shinjuku-boys-a-dykeumentary-night-screeni
 ng
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
