BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trans Day of Remembrance
DTSTART:20261120T180000
DTEND:20261120T180000
UID:a46233c15445762b31f32ab86b444bb9@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join the The 519 to commemorate the 27th anniversary of the Tr
 ans Day of Remembrance (TDoR). It’s a day to honour the lives of the Two
 -Spirit\, trans\, and non-binary siblings we have lost to transphobia\, ha
 te crimes\, illness\, substance use\, suicide\, misogyny\, institutional a
 nd legislative violence\, and murder. We&#x27\;ll honour these lives with 
 a vigil\, fellowship dinner\, community celebration\, and more. When: Frid
 ay\, November 20 Time: 6 to 8:30 p.m. Where: At The 519 and virtually via 
 Zoom This year’s theme for The 519’s TDoR event is “50 years of fier
 ce love and solidarity.” As we celebrate 50 years of The 519\, we honour
  all the trans leaders\, staff\, and community members who have poured the
 ir love\, wisdom\, rage\, hope\, and care into The 519 over the past five 
 decades to foster a space where love and solidarity fiercely exist every d
 ay. The event is free and open to all. RSVP is recommended to help us trac
 k anticipated numbers. You can also share access needs and/or request chil
 dminding during the event. Visit The519.org/tdor [Image description: A vib
 rant collage of performers at past TDoR events. Text reads: Trans Day of R
 emembrance TDoR 2026. Friday\, 20 November\, 6 p.m. at The 519 or Virtual.
  Text created with hand-made floral design reads “50 years of fierce lov
 e and solidarity”.] ‍
LOCATION:The 519 Community Centre\, 519 Church Street
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/trans-day-of-remembrance-3
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DREAMHOUSE: A Fashion Show in Honour of Trans Day of Remembrance
DTSTART:20261120T190000
DTEND:20261120T190000
UID:e069e7aad7727cd1f7ea5977478b92e2@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:DREAMHOUSE is a costume design and voguing dance program for b
 allroom youth\, culminating in a live performance to commemorate Trans Day
  of Remembrance (TDOR). &quot\;DREAMHOUSE&quot\; is a play on the Barbie D
 oll Dreamhouse\, referencing both the house structure of ballroom and the 
 ballroom vernacular term &quot\;doll.&quot\; The &quot\;doll&quot\; of PRO
 TECT THE DOLLS comes from ballroom\, not &quot\;gay slang&quot\; or &quot\
 ;Gen Z internet speak\,&quot\; but from the Black trans women who are the 
 heart of ballroom. DREAMHOUSE is a powerful tool of trans activism and art
 istry\, using creative mentorship to spotlight ballroom talent as the epic
 entre of queer arts and culture. DREAMHOUSE is led by Toronto ballroom com
 munity leaders Charlotte Carbone\, Diséiye Thompson\, Solange Alexander\,
  and Ern In Motion\, who are also multi-disciplinary artists in their resp
 ective practices of costume design and dance performance. Designers: Disé
 iye Thompson\, Char Carbone\, Fae Mulan\, Karume Unbothered\, Arsyn Pink L
 ady\, Sakura Pink Lady\, Shaddoe Pink Lady\, Thryv Old Navy Performers: Er
 n In Motion\, Solange Alexander\, Jaemy Siriano\, Krackle Old Navy\, Nicky
  007\, Vita 007\, Chess 007\, Dymund Pink Lady ‍
LOCATION:Toronto PWA Foundation\, 163 Queen St E
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/dreamhouse-a-fashion-show-in-honour-of-tra
 ns-day-of-remembrance
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
