UID:7ac5e441f1fdbc077f030cc1cc19e74b@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Queer Death Salon is a virtual community space for all 2SLGBTQ
 IA+ people to come together to discuss death\, dying and grief. End of lif
 e planning can be a daunting task\, especially for the queer community. Pa
 rticipants will learn important factors to consider when doing their own e
 nd of life planning\, review key documents\, and talk about what to expect
  when working with a funeral director when a death occurs. Ezra Salter (th
 ey/them) is a Louisiana licensed Funeral Director and Embalmer practicing 
 in New Orleans. They are co-creator of the Louisiana LGBTQ+ End of Life Pl
 anning Guide. Their professional focus includes advocacy for queer deathca
 re\, green burial options\, and the preservation of historic cemeteries. I
 n their personal life they are a proud leatherdyke working to build local 
 leather community. ‍
LOCATION:Online\, online
