BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Conditioned Instincts: The Psychology of Pet Headspace
DTSTART:20261125T200000
DTEND:20261125T200000
UID:5a39e9ba7599d00da39b17c809fb9ece@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Inside the mind of the human pet... and how to play with it! U
 S / International Attendees: This event is priced in CAD. At checkout\, yo
 u will see the CAD price\, but your bank will automatically convert it to 
 your local currency. See tickets for estimated USD conversions! Canadian L
 ocals: If you are based in Canada and experiencing financial barriers\, en
 ter promo code CANADALOCAL at checkout to unlock our $20 CAD support tier.
  --- Live on Zoom. Recording available to ticketholders for 14 days after 
 class! Get the Total Desire Pass to save on all 5 classes in the Psycholog
 y &amp\; Instinct Series! --- Have you ever wondered why you think so diff
 erently as a pet? Maybe you start to see your inner pet come out in your e
 veryday life? You may be surprised to learn how much of pet play and heads
 pace can be explained by surprisingly common psychological concepts that f
 it into your daily life (or the daily lives of your average vanilla friend
 ). Join Pup Ryder\, to learn about how various aspects of psychology play 
 a role in your headspace\, pet-self\, and dynamics\, while also learning a
 bout some psychological tips and tricks that you may be able to add in to 
 really play with your pet’s head. --- Get the Total Desire Pass to save 
 on all 5 classes in the Psychology &amp\; Instinct Series! This also inclu
 des a FREE month of the new Wolfe Academy of Desire Patreon + 15% off a on
 e-on-one coaching session. NOTE: This class will not be uploaded onto the 
 Patreon. --- About the Instructor Pup Ryder (he/him) is a member of the To
 ronto pet play community\, previously holding a role as an event organizer
 . He is currently pursuing a PhD in psychology examining the formation of 
 boundaries in power exchange relationships. His past research\, as well as
  several ongoing research projects also revolve around pet play experience
 s\, headspace\, and different roles within pet play communities. Access: T
 his class is offered live and online through Zoom. You may need to downloa
 d the free\, basic version of the Zoom app to join. The class will be reco
 rded with the recording available to ticketholders for 14 days. Zoom now p
 rovides closed captioning which will be available for this event. ‍
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/conditioned-instincts-the-psychology-of-pe
 t-headspace
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Calling All Cowgays! The Ratskin Family Band\, Trash Panda Brass &
 amp\; SPURS
DTSTART:20261126T190000
DTEND:20261126T190000
UID:4347de86d4db3c9e18a1648754299dca@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:The Ratskin Family Band\, Trash Panda Brass &amp\; SPURS lead 
 a cuntry night full of line lancing\, laughs at Supermarket Toronto 268 Au
 gusta Ave. Doors at 7:00pm Let&#x27\;s Go Girls! Gays! Theys! &amp\; Frien
 ds! The worlds first drag country band is coming to Supermarket in Kensing
 ton!! Get your boots on Toronto and prepare to dance all night with Queer 
 Line Dancing lead by SPURS SPURS: Mer &amp\; Ver have been teaching at Tor
 onto&#x27\;s beloved queer line dancing night for years\, and getting to d
 ance with crowds at live music shows is their favourite kind of SPURS spin
 off. They&#x27\;ve been best friends since college\, and have shared all k
 inds of artistic projects between them\, from Veronique costume designing 
 Meredith&#x27\;s production of Falsettos\, to co-directing and co-choreogr
 aphing CJ Wiley&#x27\;s Big Gay Musical together. They&#x27\;ll be getting
  the crowd warmed up with beginner line dances to be danced to songs durin
 g both sets of music\, so come early and cut a gay little rug! Followed by
  THE HITS (country\, pop &amp\; otherwise) played by an all-queer brass ba
 nd\, Trash Panda Brass: Trash Panda Brass formed in the summer of 2022 on 
 the streets of Toronto with a simple mission of engaging crowds and spread
 ing queer and inclusive joy. Within two years of conception\, they graced 
 the cover of Whole Note magazine\, rocked TD Jazz Fest\, DoWestFest\, Cult
 ivate festival\, and the Distillery District Concert Series. With the tale
 nts of the worlds first &amp\; only drag country band\, The Ratskin Family
  Band\, closing out the night... this sure to be an unforgettable night of
  queer cuntry magic for you &amp\; your friends Need a place to go totally
  crazy\, forget you&#x27\;re a lady\, mens shirt? short skirt? LOOK NO FUR
 THER THAN SUPERMARKET BAR AND VARIETY IN KENSINGTON MARKET ON NOVEMBER 26t
 h ‍
LOCATION:Supermarket\, 268 Augusta Ave
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/calling-all-cowgays-the-ratskin-family-ban
 d-trash-panda-brass-spurs
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Come Over: Sapphic House Party
DTSTART:20261126T190000
DTEND:20261126T190000
UID:0abec8cb6606a9ff9d0008f3b83f9137@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:You know that part of a house party when everyone somehow ends
  up in the kitchen while a few people are dancing their hearts out in the 
 living room? Someone’s pouring another drink\, someone’s telling a sto
 ry with way too much detail\, and you’re pretending you came back for a 
 little snack when really you wanted to keep talking to that cute person yo
 u just met! That’s the feeling we want you to have at Come Over. A night
  where you can show up with your friends\, make a few new ones\, and go fr
 om deep conversation to dancing in the time it takes for the DJ to play yo
 ur song. Stay for a drink\, stay for a dance\, stay because you said goodb
 ye twenty minutes ago and somehow you’re still here. And yes\, babe\, th
 ere’s food. Every edition\, Proud Palate will put out a beautiful grazin
 g board for everyone to snack on throughout the night. Have a little bite 
 when you get in\, go back for more between songs\, and use “I’m just g
 rabbing something to eat” as an excuse to walk past your crush one more 
 time. We get it. The Experience For the first two hours of every Come Over
 \, there’s a little extra you can opt into. It’s a chance to come earl
 y\, mingle a little more\, and do something different together before the 
 dance floor gets going. What will it be? Depends on the night. Maybe we’
 ll learn a few dance moves together. Maybe we’ll take a class in somethi
 ng you never thought you’d try at a house party. We’re keeping a few s
 ecrets for now\, but for our very first edition… Come Over for Dinner We
 ’re starting with risotto paired with wine\, brought to you by Proud Pal
 ate. Think a bowl of risotto\, a glass of wine\, and enough time to get pa
 st “so\, how do you know everyone?” before somebody pulls you onto the
  dance floor. Make a dinner date out of it\, come solo and meet someone ov
 er a glass of wine\, or drop by later when you’re ready to dance. The gr
 azing board will be out all night\, so there’ll still be something to sn
 ack on after dinner. Come hungry. Stay as long as you like. And\, Come Ove
 r. 💋 ‍
LOCATION:1444 Dupont St\, 1444 Dupont St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/come-over-sapphic-house-party
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
